--- body ---
## Context
Audit B7 (`docs/2026-09-24-rules-coherence-audit.md`). climate `.claude/rules/architecture.md` is scoped
`paths: "**/*"`: 277 lines effectively resident, outside any harness budget
test (`test_rules_resident_budget.py` covers `~/.claude/rules` only).

## Decision needed
Recommended: scope to the paths the body describes (`deliverables/**`,
`scripts/**`, `Makefile`, `dvc.yaml`, `config/**`, `data/**`) and move the
data-location paragraph into AGENTS.md if every session needs it.
Alternative: accept residency and extend a budget test to project rules.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Author decision logged here
- [ ] Rule scoped, or residency budgeted

## Proposal (2026-09-24): budget the project channel, not one file

Measured 2026-09-24, characters of project rules a session pays before its
first question (bodies without `paths:`, or with a catch-all glob):

| Repo | Resident project rules | chars |
|---|---|---|
| climate-finance-het | architecture.md (`**/*`), git.md, workflow.md, jetp-research.md | 28 000 |
| aedist-technical-report | workflow.md | 2 365 |
| others | none | 0 |

The harness caps its own resident rules at 36 000 chars; climate adds 78 % on
top, unwatched. `scripts/resident_census.py` says so itself: a consumer
project's own files are "not counted, because it is not in this repo".
architecture.md is one instance of a class, so the fix is general:

1. **Measure.** Extend `resident_census.py` with a project mode: for a repo,
   sum `AGENTS.md` (+ `CLAUDE.md` and its `@` chain) and every
   `.claude/rules/*.md` that is resident, counting a catch-all `paths:`
   (`**/*`, `**`, `*`) as resident — a catch-all is residency in disguise.
2. **Surface, don't gate.** The harness cannot gate a project's CI. At
   session start `prompt-project-coherence.sh` already names local sources;
   add one declarative line when the project channel exceeds a budget
   (proposed 12 000 chars) or declares a catch-all, naming the files.
3. **Doctrine, one line in `rules/README.md`:** the harness scoping rule
   applies to project rules too — scope by path when the trigger is a path;
   make it a skill when the trigger is a task (the 2026-09-09 move of
   `/pdf-finish`, `/cut-prose`, `/submission-event`).
4. **First application, climate:** split architecture.md by section onto the
   paths each describes (data location → `data/**`, `dvc.yaml`, `.env`;
   deliverable layout → `deliverables/**`; build graph → `Makefile`,
   `paths.mk`), keeping in AGENTS.md only what every session needs;
   jetp-research.md is task-triggered, so it becomes a project skill.

Decision asked: adopt 1–3 as a harness ticket and 4 as a climate ticket? The
12 000 budget is a starting point to ratchet from, not a measured optimum.
